{
  "kanda": "aranya",
  "sarga": 21,
  "title": "Surpanakha reports demons death to Khara",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga21/aranyasans21.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga21/aranyaitrans21.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Shuurpanakha comes again to her brother Khara to report that all the fourteen demons sent by him are slain by Rama. She persuades him to wage a war against Rama and Lakshmana and annihilate them for they intruded into Dandaka and there is every possibility of onslaught by them on demons."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे एक विंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 21st chapter in Aranya Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "3.21.1",
      "label": "3.21.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "स पुनः पतिताम् दृष्ट्वा क्रोधात् शूर्पणखाम् खरः |\nउवाच व्यक्तता वाचा ताम् अनर्थ अर्थम् आगताम्",
      "iast": "sa punaḥ patitām dṛṣṭvā krodhāt śūrpaṇakhām kharaḥ |\nuvāca vyak{}tatā vācā tām anartha artham āgatām",
      "translation": "On seeing Shuurpanakha who came back only to wreck havoc on demonic race and again fell before him as before, Khara spoke this sentence to her in clear terms in all his fury.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "saH kharaH",
          "iast": "saḥ kharaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सः खरः",
          "meaning": "he, Khara",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "punaH patitaam shuurpaNakhaam dR^iSTvaa",
          "iast": "punaḥ patitām śūrpaṇakhām dṛṣṭvā",
          "devanagari": "पुनः पतितां शूर्पणखां दृष्ट्वा",
          "meaning": "again, fallen - before him, Shuurpanakha, on seeing",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "anartha artham aagataam",
          "iast": "anartha artham āgatām",
          "devanagari": "अनर्थ अर्थं आगतां",
          "meaning": "calamity, for the purpose of, came back - to wreck havoc on",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "taam",
          "iast": "tām",
          "devanagari": "तां",
          "meaning": "to her",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vyaktataa vaacaa",
          "iast": "vyaktatā vācā",
          "devanagari": "व्यक्तता वाचा",
          "meaning": "in clear, words",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "krodhaat uvaaca",
          "iast": "krodhāt uvāca",
          "devanagari": "क्रोधात् उवाच",
          "meaning": "furiously, said.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.21.2",
      "label": "3.21.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "मया तु इदानीम् शूराः ते राक्षसा पिशित अशनाः |\nत्वत् प्रियार्थम् विनिर्दिष्टाः किम् अर्थम् रुद्यते पुनः",
      "iast": "mayā tu idānīm śūrāḥ te rākṣasā piśita aśanāḥ |\ntvat priyārtham vinirdiṣṭāḥ kim artham rudyate punaḥ",
      "translation": "\"What for your are howling again when I have just now commanded those fearless flesh eating demons in order to fulfill your wish?",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "mayaa",
          "iast": "mayā",
          "devanagari": "मया",
          "meaning": "by me",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tvat priya artham",
          "iast": "tvat priya artham",
          "devanagari": "त्वत् प्रिय अर्थं",
          "meaning": "your, wish, to fulfill",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "idaaniim",
          "iast": "idānīm",
          "devanagari": "इदानीं",
          "meaning": "just now",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pishita ashanaaH",
          "iast": "piśita aśanāḥ",
          "devanagari": "पिशित अशनाः",
          "meaning": "flesh, eating, demons",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shuuraaH",
          "iast": "śūrāḥ",
          "devanagari": "शूराः",
          "meaning": "fearless ones",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "te raakSasaa",
