          "iast": "bhrātaram kharam abravīt",
          "devanagari": "भ्रातरं खरं अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "to brother, Khara, she spoke.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.21.7",
      "label": "3.21.7",
      "numbers": [
        7
      ],
      "devanagari": "अस्मि इदानीम् अहम् प्रप्ता हत श्रवण नासिका |\nशोणित ओघ परिक्लिन्ना त्वया च परिसमन्विता",
      "iast": "asmi idānīm aham praptā hata śravaṇa nāsikā |\nśoṇita ogha pariklinnā tvayā ca parisamanvitā",
      "translation": "\"I came to you just a while back with my ears and nose chopped off and wet with gushes of blood, and you too have comforted me, isn't it.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "hata shravaNa naasikaa",
          "iast": "hata śravaṇa nāsikā",
          "devanagari": "हत श्रवण नासिका",
          "meaning": "having chopped, ears, nose",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aham",
          "iast": "aham",
          "devanagari": "अहं",
          "meaning": "I",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 2
