          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.21.9",
      "label": "3.21.9",
      "numbers": [
        9
      ],
      "devanagari": "ते तु रामेण सामर्षाः शूल पट्टिस पाणयः |\nसमरे निहताः सर्वे सायकैः मर्म भेदिभिः",
      "iast": "te tu rāmeṇa sāmarṣāḥ śūla paṭṭisa pāṇayaḥ |\nsamare nihatāḥ sarve sāyakaiḥ marma bhedibhiḥ",
      "translation": "\"But they all who handled their spears and bolts along with an envious anger are killed in a fight with Rama by his arrows that cleave the crucial parts of his opponents.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "sa amarSaaH",
          "iast": "sa amarṣāḥ",
          "devanagari": "स अमर्षाः",
          "meaning": "with, envious anger",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
